{
 "id": "lfo-rnd",
 "version": "1.4",
 "title": "LFO RND page",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "MrScruff (rytm-mods); elemod port: Iced-Cream",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-only",
 "description": "A second LFO page, LFO RND, reached by pressing the LFO page key again: two random modifiers per sound, each a destination (DS1/DS2, one of 16, chosen from stock's LFO DST list) and a depth (DP1/DP2, 0..64 in 16 steps). On every note trig each modifier draws a random offset for its destination, clamped to the parameter's range, held until the next note, on top of p-locks, slides and LFO 1. Stored in the sound through core-ar2 0.2's mod storage (one 16-bit sound field), so the sound's stock bytes stay stock; sounds saved by lfo-rnd 1.0 keep their settings. Port of rytm-mods 0004-lfo-rnd. From 1.2 the page goes through core-ar2 0.4's page tables and page-key lists (needs core 0.4, OS 1.74 only). From 1.3 (core-ar2 0.9) the four settings are four 4-bit sound fields, each a lockable parameter registered in core_lock_params on its page knob: DS1 and DS2 are lockable (p-locks, scene locks, MIDI) and step without smoothing; DP1 and DP2 are also LFO, velocity and aftertouch destinations (RND:Random 1 Depth, RND:Random 2 Depth). At each note's start the audio interrupt takes the four as core plays them (core_param_int: the sound's value, the trig's p-lock or the scene's lock, plus the performances, the LFO and the routes), so a p-locked or modulated depth or destination draws that note's offset. Settings saved by 1.1 and 1.2 (one 16-bit field) load as the defaults; lfo-rnd 1.0's word still loads (needs core 0.9). From 1.4 (core-ar2 0.13) the page's four knobs are the mod's own knob ids (\"knobs\": 4) in place of stock ids 1..4: no stock parameter record is patched, DS1 and DS2 draw as stock's LFO DST knob and DP1 and DP2 as a dial through core_knob_looks, and the knob draw site at 0x400a85e8, which core-ar2 0.13 takes, is gone, so it links with core-ar2 0.13 and later, flashed and from the +Drive (needs core 0.13).",
 "device": "analog-rytm-mk2",
 "os": "1.73",
